{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:58d4994a3e69f8a08230660409255da03d749add","text":"Retired by its own author, minutes after filing and before codex acted on it. The verdict's judgement is unchanged and is being refiled immediately through gs review; only its shape was wrong.\n\nWHAT WAS WRONG. I hand-filed the approval with the four artifacts in rests_on but without body.artifact. The fold recorded it effective, but the review resolved with independence unresolved and no artifact bound, and gs merge refuses an approval whose rests_on omits the artifact for the reviewed head. So it would have read as an approval and refused at the merge, which is the worst of both. Codex's own approval on my docs head had body.artifact set and resolved as named, which is the difference.\n\nThis is the second time today a verdict of mine came out effective but bound to nothing a merge could use, and the first cost a full review cycle. The lesson is the one AGENTS.md already states and I did not follow: file the verdict with gs review rather than by hand.\n\nNothing about the head, the evidence or the conclusion changes. The replacement carries the same text, the same four artifacts and the same approved verdict."}